Standardy a sady
****************

{{description: Co přesně rozhodují vestavěné presety DressCode: standardy PER Coding Style 3.1, PSR-12, Nette a Symfony a sady modernizations, deprecations, cleanup, correctness, types a compilerOptimizations, každý celým svým souborem.}}

.[perex]
Vestavěný preset je soubor téhož tvaru jako vaše konfigurace, takže nejlepší popis toho, co rozhoduje, je on sám. Tady je každý celý, i s komentáři, které říkají, proč má rozhodnutí svou hodnotu. Standardy rozhodují o vzhledu kódu a projekt si jeden vezme za základ, sady přidávají jeden záměr a dají se položit vedle kteréhokoli standardu.

Preset vychází z presetů, které jmenuje jeho klíč `use`, a mění jen to, co sám napíše; `nette` tedy stojí na `perCs` a ten na `psr12`. Co z toho všeho nakonec platí i s tím, odkud se každá hodnota vzala, vypíše `dresscode config --preset nette`. Jak se presety skládají s vaší konfigurací, popisuje stránka [Konfigurace |configuration#Standardy a sady], co znamená každý klíč, [Struktura konfigurace |decisions/@home].


Standardy
=========

Čtyři standardy rozhodují o všem, co vidíte: o odsazení, závorkách, mezerách, prázdných řádcích i zalamování. `psr12` a `perCs` jsou psané podle textu specifikací, oddíl po oddílu, a nic vlastního nepřidávají. `nette` a `symfony` stojí na PER Coding Style a přidávají, co chtějí jejich projekty.

Řádek delší než `file.lineLength` standard rozloží, kde to konstrukce na něm dovolí. Co rozložit nejde, třeba dlouhý řetězec nebo komentář, `psr12` a `perCs` jen hlásí varováním, protože PSR-12 bere limit 120 znaků jako měkký, `nette` chybou a `symfony` délku řádku nehlídá vůbec.


`psr12`
=======

[PSR-12 |https://www.php-fig.org/psr/psr-12/], oddíl po oddílu.

```neon .[preset]
# PSR-12 Extended Coding Style
#
# PSR-12, section by section; the specification defines the style and this preset adds nothing of its own.

file:
	bom: forbidden
	openingTag: '<?php'                       # not `<?` or `<?PHP`
	closingTagAtEnd: forbidden                # a `?>` before HTML stays
	lineEnding: majority                      # as most lines of the file, LF on a tie
	finalLineEndings: 1
	trailingWhitespace: forbidden             # the text of a string stays
	lineLength: 120                           # what is wider is spread
	longLines: warning                        # what nothing could spread only warns, the limit being soft
	statementsPerLine: 1                      # `foo(); bar();` takes two lines

indentation:
	unit: '4 spaces'
	binaryOperator: 0                         # `&& $b` right below `$a`, a level deeper after `$x =` or `return`
	ternary: 1                                # `?` and `:` opening a line
	switchCase: 1                             # `case` inside `switch`
	chain: flat                               # every link one level below the start of the chain

# names are reported, never renamed
naming:
	class: PascalCase
	method: camelCase                         # `__construct()` passes
	constant: UPPER_CASE

casing:
	keyword: lowercase                        # `self`, `parent` too
	trueFalseNull: lowercase
	type: lowercase                           # `int`, `string`, `void`

qualification:
	uselessBackslash: forbidden               # `use Foo\Bar;`, not `use \Foo\Bar;`

imports:
	order:
		kinds: [class, function, constant]    # the names of a kind in the order written

spacing:
	declare: 'declare(strict_types=1)'
	call: 'foo($a, $b)'                       # `function foo($a)` too
	parentheses: '($a)'
	controlKeyword: 'if ($a)'                 # `while`, `for`, `foreach`, `switch`, `catch` too
	connectingKeyword: '} else {'             # `catch`, `finally`, `as`, the `use` of a closure too
	functionKeyword: 'function ($x)'
	languageConstruct: 'return $x'            # `throw`, `yield`, `new`, `include` too
	comma: '$a, $b'
	commaAlignment: none                      # no extra spaces after a comma
	cast: '(int) $x'
	reference: '&$x'
	spread: '...$x'
	unaryOperator: '-$x'                      # `!$a`, `++$i` too
	unaryOperatorsWithSpace: [!]              # `! $x` may stay
	binaryOperator: '$a + $b'                 # `=`, `=>`, `instanceof` too
	concatenation: '$a . $b'
	ternary: '$a ? $b : $c'                   # `$a ?: $b` too
	classHead: 'class Foo extends Bar implements Baz'
	anonymousClass: 'new class ($a)'
	modifier: 'final public static function'
	typeDeclaration: '?int $x'                # `): int` too
	catchType: 'catch (A | B $e)'
	switchCase: 'case 1:'

multiline:
	signature: perLine                        # a parameter per line once spread or too wide
	signaturePromoted: asSignature            # spread only when too wide
	call: perLine                             # an argument per line once spread
	condition: perLine                        # `if (` above `$a`, `) {` below the last part
	for: perLine                              # a section of `for` per line
	binaryOperator: perLine                   # `&& $b`, `. $b` opening a line each where the line is too wide
	implements: perLine                       # an interface per line below `implements`
	operatorPosition:
		binary: lineStart                     # `+ $b` opens the line, not ends the one before
		condition: lineStart                  # `&& $b` opens the line

braces:
	position:
		class: nextLine
		function: nextLine                    # one with parameters on one line
		multilineSignature: sameLine          # `) {` on a line of their own
		closure: sameLine
		anonymousClass: sameLine
		controlStructure: sameLine
		continuingKeyword: sameLine           # `} else {`
	emptyBody: ownLines                       # not `{}`
	bracelessBody: forbidden                  # `if ($a) foo();` gets braces
	singlelineClosure: forbidden              # `function () { return 1; }` is spread

blankLines:
	afterOpeningTag: 1
	beforeNamespace: 1
	afterNamespace: 1
	afterImports: 1
	betweenImportKinds: 1
	beforeFirstMethod: 0
	afterLastMethod: 0
	beforeFirstMember: 0
	afterLastMember: 0
	betweenTraitUses: 0
	afterTraitUses: 1

classes:
	visibility:
		member: required                      # `var` is `public`
		interfaceMethod: required             # `public` though implied
	modifiers:
		order: canonical                      # `final public static`
	members:
		order: [traitUse]
		groupable: [constant]                 # `public $a, $b;` is split
	emptyParentheses:
		instantiation: required               # `new Foo()`

controlFlow:
	elseif: 'elseif'                          # not `else if`
	switch:
		caseTerminator: ':'                   # not `case 1;`
		fallThroughComment: no break          # the comment of a fall-through
	emptyStatement: forbidden                 # `foo();;`

expressions:
	cast: canonical                           # `(int)`, not `(integer)` or `( int )`
```


`perCs`
=======

[PER Coding Style 3.1 |https://www.php-fig.org/per/coding-style/], nástupce PSR-12: k němu přidává čárky na konci víceřádkových seznamů, arrow funkce, prázdná těla `{}`, atributy, výčty, heredoc a property hooky.

```neon .[preset]
# PER Coding Style 3.1
#
# PSR-12 plus what PER Coding Style added (trailing commas, short closures, empty bodies as `{}`, attributes,
# enumerations, heredoc, property hooks); the specification defines the style and this preset adds nothing of its own.

use: psr12

indentation:
	heredoc: startPlusOne                    # body and closing marker one level deeper than the start

naming:
	enumCase: PascalCase                     # reported, never renamed

spacing:
	attribute: '#[Foo($a)]'
	fnKeyword: 'fn($x) => $x'
	semicolon:
		before: '$a;'
	catchType: 'catch (A|B $e)'             # as a union type
	namedArgument: 'foo(name: $x)'

multiline:
	chain: perLine                           # a link per line once spread
	ternary: perLine                         # `?` and `:` each on a line once spread
	array: perLine                           # an item per line once spread
	operatorPosition:
		concatenation: lineStart             # `. $b` opens the line
		ternary: lineStart                   # `? $b` and `: $c` open the lines
	# a comma after the last item where the closing bracket has a line of its own, none on one line
	trailingComma:
		array: required
		argument: required
		parameter: required
		matchArm: required
		closureUse: required
		import: optional
		list: optional
	attributes:
		declaration: ownLines                # a group per line above the declaration
		parameter: ownLines                  # so in parameters spread over lines

braces:
	emptyBody: sameLine                      # `function foo(): void {}`
	emptyAnonymousClass: sameLine            # `new class {}`

classes:
	members:
		groupable: []                        # `const A = 1, B = 2;` is split
		perLine: 1
	emptyParentheses:
		anonymousClass: forbidden            # `new class {}`, not `new class() {}`
		attribute: forbidden                 # `#[Foo]`, not `#[Foo()]`

types:
	nullable: '?int'                         # not `int|null`
	nullPosition: last                       # `int|string|null`

literals:
	heredocWithoutInterpolation: forbidden   # a nowdoc `<<<'EOT'` instead
	longArraySyntax: forbidden               # `[1, 2]`, not `array(1, 2)`

phpdoc:
	aboveAttributes: required
```


`nette`
=======

[Nette Coding Standard |https://doc.nette.org/cs/contributing/coding-standard]: PER Coding Style s tabulátory a rozvržením knihoven Nette, `declare(strict_types=1)` na řádku `<?php` a hygiena kódu, kterou knihovny Nette dodržují. Kromě `perCs` používá sady `cleanup`, `types` a `correctness` a pár jejich rozhodnutí vrací hodnotou `keep`: větev `else` za `return`, ladicí volání, třídu s `__toString()` bez `Stringable`, oba zápisy typu pole a nativní typy parametrů, vlastností a návratových hodnot. Projekt, který tytéž sady napíše vedle `nette`, je zpátky nedostane, protože každá sada leží jen jednou, pod `nette`; kdo je chce, napíše ta rozhodnutí sám.

```neon .[preset]
# Nette Coding Standard
#
# PER Coding Style with tabs and the layout of the Nette libraries, the hygiene of the code, and the choices the Nette
# libraries make: strict types declared on the line of the opening tag, how names are cased, in what order the members
# of a class stand, which functions and constructs are out, and what a doc comment of theirs holds. The layout departs
# from PER Coding Style in two blank lines between methods, none inside the braces of a body, one closing a branch or
# a case another one follows when its last statement stands apart, a tab that may align commas, the brace of
# a multi-line signature below a return type, promoted properties on lines of their own, an expression on the line of
# its return, and a chain, an array or a condition that may keep the shape it has.

use:
	- perCs
	- cleanup
	- types
	- correctness

file:
	strictTypes:
		declaration: required         # risky, `'1'` passed to `int` then throws
		position: openingTagLine
	lineLength: 140                   # a tab counts as 4 columns
	longLines: forbidden
	lineLengthExcept: [imports, '~^\s*throw new ~']   # the message of an exception stays whole

indentation:
	unit: tab
	ternaryBelowCondition: stepped    # `?` and `:` one level below a multi-line condition
	chain: nested                     # a link may stand one level deeper than the one before

# names are reported, never renamed
naming:
	function: camelCase
	constant: PascalCase
	property: camelCase
	variable: camelCase
	classKindInName: forbidden        # `FooInterface`, `FooTrait`, `AbstractFoo`

casing:
	magicConstant: uppercase
	class: declared                   # `DateTime`, not `datetime`
	function: declared                # `strlen()`, not `StrLen()`
	method: declared                  # `$o->getTotal()`, not `$o->gettotal()`, with `typeAnalysis`

qualification:
	class:
		otherNamespace: imported
	currentClass: self                # `self::bar()` inside `Foo`, not `Foo::bar()`

imports:
	order:
		names: alphabetical           # classes, functions, constants, each alphabetically
	grouping:
		class: [separated, grouped]   # `use A; use B;`, a group use stays
		function: [combined, grouped] # `use function a, b;`
		constant: [combined, grouped] # `use const A, B;`

spacing:
	commaAlignment: tabs              # tabs aligning columns may stay
	semicolon:
		after: 'for ($i = 0; $i < 5; $i++)'
	unaryOperatorsWithSpace: []       # `!$x`, never `! $x`
	ternaryAlignment: none            # no extra spaces around `?` and `:`
	doubleColon: 'Foo::bar()'
	objectOperator: '$a->b()'
	offsetBrackets: '$a[0]'
	arrayBrackets: '[1, 2]'
	comment:
		marker: '// text'             # also `#` and `/* */`
		afterCode: '$a; // text'      # at least one space

multiline:
	array: asWritten                          # items may share a line
	arrayMaxWidth: 130
	callSoleArgument: hugged                  # `foo(bar(` above the arguments of `bar()`, `))` below them
	signaturePromoted: always                 # however short
	chainFirstLinks: sameLine                 # `$form->addText()` above `->setRequired()`
	condition: [perLine, compact]             # `if (` above `$a`, or `if ($a` above `&& $b`
	expressionBelowReturn: forbidden          # `return [`, not `return` above `[`
	semicolonOnOwnLine: forbidden
	trailingComma:
		matchArm: keep
		closureUse: keep

braces:
	position:
		multilineSignature: nextLineAfterReturnType   # `{` below `): Foo`, otherwise `) {`
	emptyBody: ownLines                      # not `{}` as in PER Coding Style
	emptyAnonymousClass: keep
	singlelineClosure: keep
	alternativeSyntax: forbidden             # no `if: ... endif;`

# a range `[1, 2]` leaves the choice to the author
blankLines:
	afterOpeningTag: keep
	betweenImportKinds: 0
	beforeDeclaration: 2                     # above the class of a file
	betweenDeclarations: [1, 2]              # around one among statements
	betweenMethods: 2
	betweenInterfaceMethods: 1
	betweenMembers: [0, 1]                   # members without a doc comment
	beforeDocumentedMember: 1
	afterPhpdoc: 0
	afterBlockOpeningBrace: 0
	beforeBlockClosingBrace: [0, 1]
	betweenBranches: lastStatementSetApart   # before `} else {` where the last statement stands apart
	betweenCases: lastStatementSetApart      # likewise before `case`

classes:
	visibility:
		interfaceMethod: forbidden           # public anyway
	members:
		# the methods then in the order written
		order: [traitUse, enumCase, constant, publicConstant, protectedConstant, privateConstant, publicProperty, protectedProperty, privateProperty]
		groupable: [constant]                # `const A = 1, B = 2;` may stay
	emptyParentheses:
		instantiation: forbidden             # `new Foo`, but `new Foo()->bar()`

types:
	inlineVarAnnotation: forbidden   # becomes `assert()`, risky
	declaration:                     # a type only where it says something
		parameter: keep
		property: keep
		return: keep

functions:
	innerFunctions: forbidden
	closureReturningOneExpression: forbidden         # `fn() =>` instead
	closureReturningOneExpressionNested: yes         # also one holding another closure

cleanup:
	is_null: forbidden                        # `$x === null`
	settype: forbidden                        # `$x = (int) $x`
	conversionFunctions: forbidden            # `(int) $x`, not `intval($x)`
	dirnameOfFile: forbidden                  # `__DIR__`
	classNameNotation: classKeyword           # `self::class`, `static::class`
	get_class: forbidden                      # `$o::class`
	separateIssets: forbidden                 # `isset($a, $b)`
	separateUnsets: forbidden                 # `unset($a, $b);`

controlFlow:
	switch:
		fallThroughComment: break omitted     # the comment of a fall-through
	elseAfterReturn: keep                     # may stay

expressions:
	comparison:
		loose: forbidden                      # risky
		notEquals: '!='
		yoda: forbidden                       # `$a === 1`
	assignment:
		addingOne: forbidden                  # `$i++`, not `$i += 1`
		repeatingTarget: forbidden            # `$a += $b`, not `$a = $a + $b`
	ternary:
		returningItsCondition: forbidden      # `$a ?: $b`
		testingNull: forbidden                # `$a ?? $b`
	wordLogicalOperators: forbidden
	explicitPrecedence: required              # `($a && $b) || $c`
	doubleNegation: forbidden                 # `(bool) $a`, not `!!$a`

literals:
	quotes: single
	backslashes: escaped                      # `"\\d"`, not `"\d"`
	digitSeparator:
		integer: 7                            # `1_000_000`
		fraction: 20

comments:
	singleline: '//'                          # not `#`

phpdoc:
	annotation:
		casing: canonicalCase                 # `@inheritDoc`, not `@inheritdoc`
	stars: aligned                            # below the first `*` of `/**`
	blankLines: trimmed
	property:
		comment: phpdoc                       # not `//` or `/* */`
		shape: singleline                     # `/** @var int */`
		promoted: '@var'                      # not `@param` of the constructor
	forbiddenAnnotations: [@access, @author, @copyright, @created, @license, @package, @since, @subpackage, @todo, @version]
	# `Constructor.`, `Name getter.`
	forbiddenLines: ['~^(?:(?!private|protected|static)\S+ )?(?:con|de)structor\.\z~i', '~^\S+ [gs]etter\.\z~i']
	types:
		array: keep   # both notations stay
		nullPosition: last

correctness:
	globalStatement: forbidden
	debugOutput: keep                         # may stay

upgrading:
	php:
		dollarBraceInterpolation: forbidden   # `{$name}`, not `${name}`
		implicitNullable: forbidden           # `?int $x = null`, not `int $x = null`
		backticks: forbidden                  # `shell_exec()`
	syntax:
		octalPrefix: adopted                  # `0o17`, not `017`
	classes:
		Stringable: keep                      # implied by `__toString()`

# comments that silence a decision on their line
suppressionComments:
	'~\bintentionally\s+[!=]=~': expressions.comparison.loose   # `// intentionally ==`
	'~^//\s*@\s+\S~': correctness.errorSuppression                 # `// @ why`
```


`symfony`
=========

Symfony Coding Standards tak, jak je definuje sada `@Symfony` PHP CS Fixeru, zatím bez většiny jejích pravidel pro phpDoc.

```neon .[preset]
# Symfony Coding Standards
#
# The Symfony Coding Standards as the @Symfony rule set of PHP CS Fixer defines them, without most of its rules about
# phpDoc, of which it takes only an empty doc comment, the trimming and the canonical types: PER Coding Style, which the
# set builds on, with the casing, the imports, the blank lines and the whitespace Symfony adds, and without the rules
# that would break a construct over lines, which Symfony leaves to the author.

use: perCs

file:
	lineLength: none
	longLines: keep

indentation:
	binaryOperator: keep
	chain: keep
	heredoc: keep                             # heredoc_indentation belongs to another set

casing:
	magicConstant: uppercase
	class: declared                           # `DateTime`, not `datetime`
	function: declared                        # `strlen()`, not `StrLen()`

# global_namespace_import imports nothing: a class is written with the backslash, a function and a constant too where
# they are qualified, and a bare one stays bare
qualification:
	class:
		global: backslashed                   # `\DateTime`
	function:
		global: [backslashed, bare]           # `\strlen()` or `strlen()`, never imported
	constant:
		global: [backslashed, bare]

imports:
	order:
		names: alphabetical                   # classes, functions, constants, each alphabetically
	grouping: separated                        # `use A; use B;`, not `use A, B;` or `use Acme\{A, B};`
	unused: forbidden

spacing:
	fnKeyword: 'fn ($x) => $x'
	commaAlignment: any                       # aligning spaces and tabs may stay
	semicolon:
		after: 'for ($i = 0; $i < 5; $i++)'
	unaryOperatorsWithSpace: []               # `!$x`, never `! $x`
	binaryOperatorAlignment: none             # no extra spaces around an operator
	concatenation: '$a.$b'
	objectOperator: '$a->b()'
	offsetBrackets: '$a[0]'
	arrayBrackets: '[1, 2]'
	anonymousClass: 'new class($a)'
	comment:
		marker: '// text'                     # also `#` and `/* */`
		afterCode: '$a; // text'              # at least one space

multiline:
	signature: keep
	# no fixer of the set breaks a chain, a condition, a ternary or an array
	call: keep
	chain: keep
	condition: keep
	for: keep
	binaryOperator: keep
	ternary: keep
	array: keep
	implements: keep
	operatorPosition:
		# operator_linebreak moves only a boolean operator, which no option here tells from the others
		binary: keep
		concatenation: keep
		ternary: keep
		condition: keep
	trailingComma:
		argument: optional                    # may stay or not where spread, never on one line
		closureUse: keep
	attributes:
		parameter: keep

braces:
	emptyBody: ownLines                       # not `{}` as in PER Coding Style
	emptyAnonymousClass: keep
	singlelineClosure: keep
	bareStatementGroup: forbidden             # no `{ ... }` that nothing opens
	alternativeSyntax: forbidden              # no `if: ... endif;`

# a range `[0, 1]` leaves the choice to the author, `[1, null]` is one or more
blankLines:
	betweenDeclarations: [0, 1]               # around one among statements
	betweenMethods: 1
	betweenInterfaceMethods: 1
	betweenTraitUses: keep
	afterTraitUses: keep
	afterPhpdoc: 0
	beforeStatement: {return: [1, null]}      # a `return` set apart from the code above it

classes:
	untypedPropertyNullInitialization: forbidden   # `public $a;`, not `public $a = null;`

functions:
	trailingBareReturn: forbidden             # no `return;` closing a function

controlFlow:
	elseAfterReturn: forbidden                # the `else` after a `return` goes, its body following the `if`

expressions:
	comparison:
		notEquals: '!='                       # not `<>`
	assignment:
		addingOne: forbidden                  # `$i++`, not `$i += 1`
	doubleNegation: forbidden                 # `(bool) $a`, not `!!$a`
	parenthesesAfterConstruct: forbidden      # `return $x;`, not `return ($x);`

literals:
	quotes: single
	heredocWithoutInterpolation: keep         # heredoc_to_nowdoc belongs to another set

comments:
	singleline: '//'                          # not `#`
	empty: forbidden

phpdoc:
	blankLines: trimmed
	empty: forbidden
	types:
		builtin: canonical                    # `int`, not `integer`, each type of a union once
		nullPosition: last

correctness:
	continueInSwitch: forbidden               # a `continue` only leaving a `switch`, reported

upgrading:
	php:
		dollarBraceInterpolation: forbidden   # `{$name}`, not `${name}`
		implicitNullable: forbidden           # `?int $x = null`, not `int $x = null`
		backticks: forbidden                  # `shell_exec()`
```


Sady
====

Sada nerozhoduje nic o vzhledu kódu, a proto se se standardem nikdy nepere. Pokládá se vedle něj (`use: [nette, modernizations]`) a hlavně roste: rozhodnutí, které DressCode v nové verzi získá, přibude do své sady, a projekt, který ji rozšiřuje, ho dostane bez změny konfigurace.


`modernizations`
================

Konstrukce novějšího PHP tam, kde totéž říká starší zápis, každá až od verze, kterou cíl projektu dovolí, a novější zápis, který nabízejí soubory dat nainstalovaných balíčků.

```neon .[preset]
# Modernizations
#
# The construct a newer PHP has, written where an older one says the same, each where the target version of the
# project has it, and the newer form the upgrading files of the installed packages offer. It decides nothing about the
# layout, so it goes with any standard.

functions:
	closureReturningOneExpression: forbidden         # `fn() =>` instead
	closureReturningOneExpressionNested: yes         # also one holding another closure

cleanup:
	classNameNotation: classKeyword            # `self::class`, `static::class`
	separateIssets: forbidden                  # `isset($a, $b)`
	separateUnsets: forbidden                  # `unset($a, $b);`

controlFlow:
	ifElseReturning: forbidden                 # `return $c ? 1 : 2;`

expressions:
	assignment:
		repeatingTarget: forbidden             # `$a += $b`, not `$a = $a + $b`
	ternary:
		testingNull: forbidden                 # `$a ?? $b`
		returningItsCondition: forbidden       # `$a ?: $b`

literals:
	longArraySyntax: forbidden                 # `[1, 2]`, not `array(1, 2)`

upgrading:
	libraries:
		packages: adopted                      # as the upgrading files of the packages say
	php:
		sleepAndWakeup: forbidden              # `__serialize()` and `__unserialize()` instead
	syntax:
		spreadForArrayMerge: adopted           # `[...$a, ...$b]`, not `array_merge($a, $b)`
		dynamicClassConstant: adopted          # `X::{$name}`, not `constant("X::$name")`
		match: adopted                         # for a `switch` returning or assigning
		throwExpression: adopted               # `$a ?? throw new E`
		cloneWith: adopted                     # `clone($o, [...])`
		nullsafe: adopted                      # `$a?->b`, not `$a ? $a->b : null`
		pipe: adopted                          # `$x |> a(...) |> b(...)`, not `b(a($x))`
		newWithoutWrapping: adopted            # `new Foo()->bar()`, not `(new Foo())->bar()`
		firstClassCallables: adopted           # `foo(...)`, not `Closure::fromCallable('foo')`
		octalPrefix: adopted                   # `0o17`, not `017`
		newInInitializer: adopted              # `Clock $c = new SystemClock`, not a `null` swapped in the body
		promotedProperties: adopted
	functions:
		array_is_list: adopted
		arraySearchFunctions: adopted          # `array_find()`, `array_any()` for a `foreach`
		arrayFirstLast: adopted                # `array_first()`, not `reset()`
		clamp: adopted                         # `clamp($x, $lo, $hi)`, not `max($lo, min($x, $hi))`
		get_debug_type: adopted
		json_validate: adopted                 # not `json_decode()` only testing
		substringFunctions: adopted            # `str_contains()`, not `strpos() !== false`
		roundingMode: adopted                  # `RoundingMode::HalfAwayFromZero`, not `PHP_ROUND_HALF_UP`
	phpdoc:
		deprecated: adopted                    # `#[\Deprecated]`, not `@deprecated`
```


`deprecations`
==============

Co novější PHP zavrhlo nebo zrušilo, opravené tam, kde náhrada existuje, a ohlášené tam, kde ne, a co soubory dat nainstalovaných balíčků uvádějí jako zavržené.

```neon .[preset]
# Deprecations
#
# What a newer PHP deprecated or removed, fixed where a replacement exists and reported where none does, and what the
# upgrading files of the installed packages list as retired. A deprecation is reported whatever the target, the code
# meeting it wherever it runs on the version that made it.

classes:
	overriding:
		signature: asAncestor                 # a child matching a parent changed by an upgrade
		parameterName: asAncestor

controlFlow:
	switch:
		caseTerminator: colon                 # `case 1:`, not `case 1;`, PHP 8.5

expressions:
	cast: canonical                           # `(int)`, not `(integer)`, PHP 8.5

# what a library or PHP breaks in a major version, reported
correctness:
	finalParent: forbidden                    # a class extending a final one
	unimplementedAbstractMethods: forbidden
	__serialize: required                     # beside `Serializable`, PHP 8.1

upgrading:
	libraries:
		packages: adopted                     # as the upgrading files of the packages say
	declarations:
		deprecatedClass: replaced             # by what `@deprecated` names
		deprecatedMember: replaced
	php:
		nullArrayKey: forbidden               # `['' => 1]`, not `[null => 1]`, PHP 8.5
		implicitNullable: forbidden           # `?int $x = null`, not `int $x = null`, PHP 8.4
		deprecatedCall: forbidden             # `mb_convert_encoding()`, not `utf8_encode()`
		constructorReturnValue: forbidden     # PHP 8.6
		sleepAndWakeup: forbidden             # `__serialize()`, PHP 8.5
		returnInFinally: forbidden            # PHP 8.6
		csvEscapeArgument: required           # the `escape` of `fgetcsv()` written out, PHP 8.4
		dollarBraceInterpolation: forbidden   # `{$name}`, not `${name}`, PHP 8.2
		reservedNames: forbidden              # `let`, `is`, `_`, PHP 8.6
		backticks: forbidden                  # `shell_exec()`, PHP 8.5
	syntax:
		firstClassCallables: adopted          # `foo(...)`, not `Closure::fromCallable('foo')`
```


`cleanup`
=========

Kód, který je tam pro nic: co opakuje, co jazyk už říká, co se nikdy nevykoná, alias funkce, komentář, který nic neříká.

```neon .[preset]
# Cleanup
#
# Code that is there for nothing: what repeats what the language already says, what can never run, an alias of a
# function, a comment or a doc comment that says nothing. It decides nothing about the layout, so it goes with any
# standard.

qualification:
	uselessBackslash: forbidden              # `use Foo\Bar;`, not `use \Foo\Bar;`
	inFileWithoutNamespace: bare             # `strlen()`, not `\strlen()`

imports:
	unused: forbidden
	aliasEqualToName: forbidden              # `use Foo;`, not `use Foo as Foo;`
	fromCurrentNamespace: forbidden            # `use Acme\Shop\Order;` in `namespace Acme\Shop`

braces:
	bareStatementGroup: forbidden            # no `{ ... }` that nothing opens

classes:
	modifiers:
		implied: forbidden                         # `final` in a final class
	untypedPropertyNullInitialization: forbidden   # `public $a;`, not `public $a = null;`
	methodOnlyCallingParent: forbidden             # one only forwarding to `parent::`, risky
	ReturnTypeWillChange: forbidden                # on a method declaring its return type

functions:
	trailingBareReturn: forbidden            # no `return;` closing a function
	uselessParameterDefault: forbidden       # a default before a required parameter

cleanup:
	aliasFunctions: [internal, imap, pg]     # `count()`, not `sizeof()`
	strlenEmptyTest: forbidden               # `$s === ''`, not `strlen($s) === 0`
	call_user_func: forbidden                # `$f($x)`, not `call_user_func($f, $x)`, risky
	__invoke: forbidden                      # `$f($x)`, not `$f->__invoke($x)`
	redundantArguments: forbidden            # `json_encode($a)`, not `json_encode($a, 0)`
	catchWithoutVariable: required           # `catch (E)` where `$e` is not read
	repeatedCatch: forbidden                 # `catch (A|B $e)` for two catches of one body

controlFlow:
	emptyStatement: forbidden                # `foo();;`
	ifReturningTrueFalse: forbidden          # `return $a > 1;` for an `if` returning `true` or `false`
	elseAfterReturn: forbidden               # the `else` after a `return` goes, its body following the `if`

expressions:
	parenthesesAfterConstruct: forbidden     # `return $x;`, not `return ($x);`
	ternary:
		ofTrueAndFalse: forbidden            # `$a > 1`, not `$a > 1 ? true : false`

literals:
	classNameInString: forbidden             # `Order::class`, not `'Acme\Shop\Order'`
	concatenatedLiterals:
		sameLine: joined                     # `'ab'`, not `'a' . 'b'`

comments:
	empty: forbidden

phpdoc:
	empty: forbidden
	constantVar: forbidden                   # a bare `@var int` on a class constant
	repeatingNativeTypes: forbidden          # one only repeating the signature
	inheritdocOnly: forbidden                # one holding only `{@inheritDoc}`

correctness:
	debugOutput: commentedOut                # `// var_dump($a);`, risky

upgrading:
	php:
		deprecatedCall: forbidden            # a call doing nothing on the target, as `curl_close()`, goes
	syntax:
		newWithoutWrapping: adopted          # `new Foo()->bar()`, not `(new Foo())->bar()`
		readonlyProperties: adopted          # `readonly` on one only the constructor writes
		readonlyClasses: adopted             # `readonly class` for a final one whose every property is
```


`correctness`
=============

To, co je nejspíš chyba, ať je styl jakýkoli.

```neon .[preset]
# Correctness
#
# What is most likely a mistake whatever the style: a call comparing loosely where it should not, `$this` where no
# object is, a `catch` nothing reaches, a doc comment contradicting itself, invisible characters in the code.

phpdoc:
	annotation:
		paramOfMissingParameter: forbidden      # a `@param` of no parameter
		duplicateReturn: forbidden
		empty: forbidden                        # `@param`, `@return`, `@var`, `@see` without content
		duplicateVar: forbidden

correctness:
	__debugInfo: array                          # `[]`, not `null`
	thisOutsideObject: forbidden                # in a static method or a function, reported
	__set_state: static
	continueInSwitch: forbidden                 # a `continue` only leaving a `switch`, reported
	unreachableCatch: forbidden                 # after `catch (Throwable)`
	exceptionWhereThrowableBelongs: forbidden   # `catch (Exception)` where `Throwable` is meant, reported
	errorSuppression: forbidden                 # the `@` operator, reported
	invisibleCharacters: forbidden              # zero-width, no-break and bidi characters, escaped
	strictComparisonArgument: required          # `in_array($a, $b, true)`, risky
	trailingWhitespaceInString: forbidden       # in a multi-line string or inline HTML
	consecutivePhpdocs: forbidden               # the first of two is lost, reported
	repeatedAssignment: forbidden               # `$a = $a = 1`
```


`types`
=======

Typy zapsané tam, kde je čte PHP.

```neon .[preset]
# Types
#
# Types written where PHP reads them: a native type on every parameter, property and return that has one, the
# shortest notation of a type, `never` on a function that only throws, `Stringable` on a class with `__toString()`.

types:
	declaration:
		parameter: required        # from `@param`, risky
		property: required         # from `@var`, risky
		return: required           # from `@return`, `void` where nothing returns, risky
	nullable: questionMark         # `?int`, not `int|null`
	nullPosition: last             # `int|string|null`

phpdoc:
	types:
		builtin: canonical         # `int`, not `integer`, each type of a union once
		array: generic             # `array<int>`, not `int[]`

upgrading:
	syntax:
		neverReturnType: adopted   # on a function that always throws
	classes:
		Stringable: adopted        # on a class with `__toString()`
```


`compilerOptimizations`
=======================

Globální funkce a konstanty ve tvaru, který PHP optimalizuje už při překladu, viz [Optimalizace funkcí a konstant |optimizations].

```neon .[preset]
# Compiler optimizations
#
# Global names written in the form PHP optimizes when it compiles the code: a function the compiler turns into an
# opcode and a constant it computes with are imported, so that the compiler knows them, and every other global name is
# written bare.

qualification:
	function:
		global: bare                                # `array_map()`, reached by the fallback at run time
		optimized: imported                         # `use function strlen;`, its arguments positional
	constant:
		global: bare                                # `E_ALL`
		optimized: [imported, backslashed]          # `PHP_VERSION_ID` imported or `\PHP_VERSION_ID`
```
